<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ terms of trade improve in March qtr.</title>
<headline>NZ terms of trade improve in March qtr.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand's terms of trade rose by 0.4 percent from the December 1996 quarter to the March 1997 quarter, Statistics New Zealand said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The terms of trade index is now 2.0 percent lower than in the March 1996 quarter, it added.</p>
<p>    Petroleum and products		+10.5		+4.6</p>
<p>    Non-fuel crude materials	    -0.1		 +0.6</p>
<p>    Plastics, plastic articles	  -0.3		 -4.4</p>
<p>    Textile yarn, fabric		  -5.0		 +1.8</p>
<p>    Iron and steel			  -3.7		 -2.8</p>
<p>    Non-electrical machinery	    -0.8		 -3.0</p>
<p>    Electrical machinery		  -5.7		 +0.6</p>
<p>    Transport equipment		   -2.2		 -0.9</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Main export price changes  (percentage)</p>
<p>						Mch qtr	    Dec qtr</p>
<p>    Dairy products			  -3.9		 -4.7</p>
<p>    Meat, wool, byproducts total	+0.4		 -3.5</p>
<p>    Fish, fish preparations	     -1.4		 -1.8</p>
<p>    Food and beverages		    -0.8		 -4.3</p>
<p>    Forestry products		     -4.7		 -2.9</p>
<p>    Non-fuel crude materials	    -0.3		 -2.8</p>
<p>    Aluminium				 +7.6		 -7.4</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
